# CLI deploys upload the working folder; leave out what the build never needs.
# Keep public/ in the upload: for a Flask project Vercel serves only the public/ files that were uploaded
# (the build overwrites them but does not add new ones). So run `npm --prefix web run build` right before
# `vercel deploy`: the same lockfile gives the same hashed names on Vercel, and nothing goes missing.
.venv/
web/node_modules/
synth/out/
test-results/
playwright-report/
.env*
